  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 220.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": [
    "The complete original core sheet, split source and all four selected singleton sources were actually viewed in native light and dark mattes. Only blink/think from core, greet/left/aha from split, and the fresh right/cheer/species singles are selected; visibly wrong extra-flipper historical cells elsewhere in old sources are not accepted.",
    "All five maximum220px both-matte pages were actually viewed with adopted neutral and all nine selected poses. Brown dot eyes/closed lid, oval cream muzzle, whiskers, small ear, clean two-tone torso outline, two connected front flippers and paired rear-flipper projection stay complete and readable, with no visible pigment smudge, duplicated front flipper, halo cloud or clipping in the selected set.",
    "Quiet blink keeps the adopted sitting body and head nearly unchanged. Greet/left/aha lift the connected far front flipper, while right turns the head to viewer right without adding a pointing limb. Think lowers the head, cheer lifts both front flippers with a deliberate slight leaned-back rounded body, and the fresh species_b has only two front flippers rather than the old extra appendage.",
    "All seven decoded recipe rows were actually viewed. Species pair intentionally turns the head right then left while lifting/lowering the existing far flipper. Body-center registration is coherent through those discrete neighbors; there is no fake tail/ground anchor or unexpected whole-body rise."
  ],
  "cautions": [
    "Cheer has a shorter visible neck and somewhat smaller face silhouette because of the active leaned-back arm-raise pose; it remains the same character and is recorded separately from the near-stable idle blink. Real-time timing should still be checked in the production clip.",
    "The stock review is native/max-use/static discrete only. No physical UI zoom/density measurement, real-time/interpolated animation or finished compressed MP4 acceptance is claimed."
  ],
